import os,json,pathlib,urllib.request
p=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
brief="""Return ONLY one Python function def blade(kind, sign): (no markdown, no notes). For existing CadQuery 2.8 build.py with global SHEET=0.6, cq, math, HALF_CHORD, no other dependencies. It replaces existing hourglass aluminum blade. Each station should visually match airship photo: 9 overlapping asymmetric upper and lower half-ellipse scaly curved silvery fins fixed about a horizontal hinge bar (axis +Y). Reference geometry target body span 385mm and total thickness ~103mm, upper 65mm above pivot and lower 37mm below, slightly taper toward nose. Axis height z=116. The original PHOTO has broad, unbroken upper round fan shapes and shallow glowing lower scoops; spindle must be visible at z near0, not a giant unsightly waist notch.
Set upper heights arrays [65,62,55,41,22] and lower depths arrays [37,35,31,24,13], for abs station kind 0..4; mirrored x positions automatically handled by caller. Upper/lower plates are two separate sheet regions. For each half create 0.6mm thick CAD sheet loft as collection of rectangular cross-section wires in local x and y: local z from 8 to +height for top, and -depth to -8 for bottom. Upper width along X at top tapers to zero smoothly elliptical, starts large at inner bottom, lower similarly. On view at y negative, create smooth scalloped sheet like a sail/zeppelin segment with the left boundary starting near hinge x=-12, and right boundary extending toward x=55 at middle/top; choose x-span to be visually 60-85mm wide. At z=8 top, leave center 8mm strip near root x+-9 for sheet clamp bolts at local z=+7, and at z=-8 near z=-7 screw; adjust if necessary. Physically no disconnected floating pieces: attach both plates to a slim solid common root bridge behind spine (between z=-8..+8 and width 10mm x) at same y, so loft sections meet root (the 2 half sheets and bridge can be fused), or if making a single body easier loft all sections continuously with an x-width profile. This function must return a *valid CadQuery Shape* with positive volume, include all 3 through-bores at x0,z=-7,0,+7 along y exactly like existing code, preserve y=sign*(24+rise) root; depth curvature from center to tips 5-7mm one-sided cylindrical in YZ across z with 0.6 sheet thickness. Current hub at x+-5.7 z+-9, y sign 21.35, sheets at y sign24 root; avoid neighbor hub. Important max overhang side silhouette should be around ~80px/adjacent 40.84mm pitch; free form approx 1.7 pitch (70mm), smooth edges.
Make robust production-valid real solids via cq.Solid.makeLoft(sections,ruled=True). No comments. Keep whole function <=85 lines. Use body of one sheet connected via narrow central region even if aesthetically black spine overlay eventually hides it. Do not use fake image outputs or pretend mechanically proven.
"""
body={"model":"gpt-6.2-astra","reasoning":{"effort":"high"},"max_output_tokens":7000,"input":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":brief}]}]}
try:
 req=urllib.request.Request("https://api.openai.com/v1/responses",data=json.dumps(body).encode(),headers={"Authorization":"Bearer "+os.environ["OPENAI_API_KEY"],"Content-Type":"application/json"},method="POST")
 with urllib.request.urlopen(req,timeout=230) as r:data=json.load(r)
 out="\n".join(c.get("text","") for row in data.get("output",[]) for c in row.get("content",[]) if c.get("type")=="output_text").strip()
 if out.startswith(chr(96)*3):out=out.split("\n",1)[1].rsplit(chr(96)*3,1)[0]
 (p/"blade_astra.py").write_text(out,encoding="utf-8")
 print("MODEL",data.get("model"),"STATUS",data.get("status"),"TOKENS",data.get("usage"),"CHARS",len(out),"HEAD",out[:390].encode("ascii","replace").decode(),flush=True)
except Exception as e:print("ERROR",type(e).__name__,str(e)[:500],flush=True)
